        "date": "2026-11-09T00:33:24Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(world): finish flecs' OS API setup once, before the first world\n\nflecs keeps its OS API (malloc, free, abort, the clock) in one\nprocess-global C struct, and the first world fills it in without a lock.\nflecs_ecs's ensure_initialized writes it after its claim mutex is\nreleased, while ecs_mini copies the struct and writes it back. Two test\nthreads building their first worlds at once could therefore copy a\nhalf-written struct. Then ecs_mini aborted on the ECS_MISSING_OS_API\ncheck (SIGABRT, flecs.c:21288, captured under lldb) or called a NULL\nhook (SIGSEGV).\n\nnew_world now runs ensure_initialized behind a std::sync::Once before it\nbuilds any world, so the struct is complete and marked initialised\nbefore any concurrent construction reads it.\n\nStress results, scripting suite, 8 copies x --test-threads=32: 7 crashes\nin 1200 runs before the fix, 0 in 1600 after. The new world_init_race\nbinary re-runs itself as children that release 32 threads at a barrier\non loaded cores: 6 crashed children in 1920 before, 0 in 3840 after.\n\nFixes #379\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
